Subject: [PATCH] kernel_flash: isolate each massflash initrd working tree

generate_flash_initrd() reuses the parent's working_dir for every massflash
instance. The second invocation extracts over the first initrd, encounters
an existing usr/share/misc directory, and aborts. Making mkdir idempotent
alone would retain stale files and append multiple instance configurations.

Allocate a fresh child working directory on every invocation and shadow
working_dir locally. This also handles repeated calls for instance zero.
The existing parent cleanup retains ownership of all temporary children.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/tools/kernel_flash/l4t_initrd_flash_internal.sh b/tools/kernel_flash/l4t_initrd_flash_internal.sh
--- a/tools/kernel_flash/l4t_initrd_flash_internal.sh
+++ b/tools/kernel_flash/l4t_initrd_flash_internal.sh
@@ -466,6 +466,13 @@
 generate_flash_initrd()
 {
 	local dev_instance="$1"
 
+	# Repeated massflash calls must not share an extracted initrd tree.
+	# Parent cleanup still owns every uniquely allocated child directory.
+	local initrd_working_dir
+	initrd_working_dir="$(mktemp -d \
+		"${working_dir}/flash-initrd-${dev_instance}.XXXXXX")" || return
+	local working_dir="${initrd_working_dir}"
+
 	pushd "${working_dir}"
 
